# The Docker build context (Dockerfile) is an allowlist: everything is out, and only what the image is built
# from comes back in. A new folder, a .env, a keystore or a Firebase file cannot slip into an image by accident.
# apps/server/test/deploy.test.ts checks this list against the files the builds actually read.
#
# Left out on purpose:
# - apps/mobile, its package.json included: with it, `npm ci` for the server would install Expo (Dockerfile).
# - apps/admin/dist and apps/server/dist: the image builds both itself, so a stale local build never ships.

*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.base.json

!packages/engine/package.json
!packages/engine/tsconfig*.json
!packages/engine/src
!packages/engine/data
!packages/protocol/package.json
!packages/protocol/tsconfig*.json
!packages/protocol/src

!apps/server/package.json
!apps/server/tsconfig.json
!apps/server/src
!apps/server/drizzle
# The blocked-words list for display names: bundled into dist/index.cjs (src/accounts/blockedWords.ts).
!apps/server/data

!apps/admin/package.json
!apps/admin/tsconfig*.json
!apps/admin/index.html
!apps/admin/vite.config.ts
!apps/admin/public
!apps/admin/src

# Out again, inside the folders above: tests, local files and anything that looks like a secret.
**/node_modules
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.data
**/google-services.json
**/GoogleService-Info.plist
**/service-account*.json
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/*.p8
**/*.p12
**/*.pem
**/*.key
